  "prefLabel": "We 101.37 Schedule 40",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "We 101.37 “Schedule 40” means the American National Standards Institute (ANSI) designation schedule number 40 for pipes and fittings computed according to the following formula: Schedule Number = (1000)(P/S) where P = internal working pressure in psig; S = allowable stress of piping material at operating conditions in psi.\n\nSource. #7306, eff 6-13-00; ss by #9177, eff 6-13-08); renumbered by #12075 (formerly We 101.33)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/we100-1000.html"
